{
  "summary": "The billing failures stem from three distinct architectural breaks: (1) Duplicate activation fees are caused by non-idempotent interface handling during a restart or re-trigger, where the one-time charge event was resent and accepted twice by CI; (2) Usage miscalculation likely results from incorrect tier mapping or missing mediation de-duplication, leading to rated quantities that do not match the 150 GB allowance threshold; (3) FI-CA posting failures indicate a break in the billing-to-accounting interface, often due to missing master data (contract account) or validation errors in the billable items (BITs) preventing the creation of receivables. Remediation requires targeted reprocessing of only error/unbilled items, leveraging BIT status to prevent duplication, and correcting the interface idempotency controls.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Root Cause Analysis: Duplicate Activation Fees",
      "module": "CC"
    },
    {
      "title": "Root Cause Analysis: Usage Miscalculation",
      "module": "CC"
    },
    {
      "title": "Root Cause Analysis: FI-CA Posting Failures",
      "module": "FI-CA"
    },
    {
      "title": "Diagnosis and Remediation Strategy",
      "module": "General"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "text": "Duplicate billing of one-time activation fees often occurs when an interface restart causes the sender to resend an event without receiving an acknowledgement, and the receiver (CI) accepts both instances because it lacks idempotency controls.",
      "citations": [
        "a321d435-80e8-43a1-a84b-1eceba44aab7"
      ],
      "identifiers_used": [],
      "module": "CC",
      "support": "direct"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "text": "The activation charge is a one-time charge triggered by the contract activation event in CC, which flows to CI as a billable item; if the event is resent, CI may create duplicate billable items unless source references are checked for uniqueness.",
      "citations": [
        "7af27ef4-d828-498a-b919-8705d4d5941b",
        "8d8decee-3108-43a4-9253-f190b64df8b8"
      ],
      "identifiers_used": [],
      "module": "CC",
      "support": "inferred"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "text": "Usage charges are rated per chargeable item from mediation; miscalculation can occur if the mediation layer fails to de-duplicate events or if CC rates against the wrong tariff tier, resulting in incorrect quantities or prices.",
      "citations": [
        "1ad1a24f-3b4f-46a8-8c14-343928fe05eb",
        "5b7d6143-1027-43ce-99e9-a1e007639280"
      ],
      "identifiers_used": [],
      "module": "CC",
      "support": "direct"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "text": "FI-CA posting failures can be caused by billable items (BITs) stuck in 'raw' status due to validation errors such as missing contract account, invalid item type, or wrong currency, preventing the creation of receivables.",
      "citations": [
        "728c43dd-211d-439f-b36b-f36ad97120cb"
      ],
      "identifiers_used": [],
      "module": "FI-CA",
      "support": "direct"
    }]}

